 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A Bosch dishwasher that won't drain usually has a blockage in the filter area, something caught in the pump impeller, or a kinked hose. The most common fix is clearing the filter and sump. Please switch off and unplug the machine first. Remove the lower rack, twist and lift out the main filter at the bottom of the tub, rinse it under the tap, and check the sump underneath for any debris like glass or food. Let me know if you found anything blocked there.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. cleaned it, drains fine now, E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. The E:24 code was simply the machine telling you it couldn't pump out because of that blockage, so clearing the filter and sump has done the trick. To help prevent this from happening again, try scraping large food scraps into the bin before loading and check for small items like glass or bones occasionally. If it starts acting up again in a few weeks, let me know, but otherwise you should be good to go."
  }
 ],
